  <p>
    The simplicity of this state machine is deceptive. The interactions between
    these states, driven by RPC calls (<code
      class="bg-surface text-primary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-sm font-mono text-[15px] border border-border-color"
      >RequestVote</code
    > and <code
      class="bg-surface text-primary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-sm font-mono text-[15px] border border-border-color"
      >AppendEntries</code
    >), are where the actual consensus is forged.
  </p>
  <h3 class="font-display text-[24px] font-semibold text-text-main mt-12 mb-4">
    Log Replication
  </h3>
  <p>
    Once a Leader is elected, it begins accepting client requests. Each request
    is a command to be executed by the replicated state machines. The Leader
    appends the command to its log as a new entry, then issues <code
      class="bg-surface text-primary px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-sm font-mono text-[15px] border border-border-color"
      >AppendEntries</code
    > RPCs in parallel to each of the other servers to replicate the entry.
  </p>
  <!-- Image Figure -->
  <figure class="my-12">
    <div class="border border-border-color p-1 bg-surface">
      <img
        alt="Abstract representation of distributed network nodes"
        class="w-full h-auto object-cover img-grayscale max-h-[400px]"
        data-alt="Server rack network cables"
